Under section 14 of the Sales Tax Act, 1990, the following persons carrying on taxable activities must register if not already registered:

- A manufacturer not operating a cottage industry;
- A retailer liable to pay sales tax, excluding retailers who pay it through electricity bills under section 3(9);
- An importer;
- An exporter intending to claim a sales tax refund on zero-rated supplies;
- A wholesaler, dealer, or distributor; and
- Anyone required by another federal or provincial law to register for a duty or tax collected or paid as a sales tax levy.

Additionally, every person—including a non-resident—selling digitally ordered goods from within Pakistan through an online marketplace, website, or software application must register, except cottage industries and retailers paying sales tax through electricity bills.

An online marketplace or courier involved in supplying such goods cannot facilitate e-commerce transactions unless the seller has an NTN and, where applicable, sales tax registration.
Sources:
- Sales Tax Act, 1990 (Same as on the official website of FBR dated 30-06-2025), pp. 5, 45 — https://pakistancode.gov.pk/pdffiles/administratorf6d20932403661e059756ab223d8542b.pdf (text retrieved 2026-08-07)
- 2022 LHC 8015 — CIR MULTAN VS M/S USMAN TRADE LINKER MULTAN (Mr. Justice Muhammad Sajid Mehmood Sethi) — https://sys.lhc.gov.pk/appjudgments/2022LHC8015.pdf (text retrieved 2026-08-10)

